Rakshita, [recipient of] his blessing;
Lhodrakpa, who held his lineage;
Gungthangpa, [recipient of] his blessing;
the one who became Mila's son of the heart,
the fully qualified lord, the precious teacher:
to the teachers of the lineage I prostrate. [N-A002](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a002) [N-A005](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a005) [N-A038](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a038)

Those to reject also have four aspects:
clinging at the time of the cause;
at the time of the dominant [condition], being taken in by a misguided spiritual friend;
at the time of the object of focus, delusion;
and at the time of the immediate [condition],
falling into the two: hope and fear. [N-A018](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a018) [N-A019](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a019)

For reliance on a qualified student,
the teacher spoke of four subdivisions:
not clinging at the time of the cause;
at the time of the dominant condition,
being taken in hand by a spiritual friend;
no delusion in the condition of the object of focus;
and at the time of the immediate [condition],
freedom from the two: hope and fear. [N-A002](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a002) [N-A018](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a018) [N-A019](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a019) [N-A027](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a027) [N-A038](../translations/NOTES.md#n-a038)
